# v0.2.0 certificate evidence — sha256 of the two green gate-p5 logs, one per ISA.
# Both measured at -test.count=30, on-demand full-size judged instances in us-east-1.
#
# The amd64 leg was judged at 0821366 and the arm64 leg at 49165ca. The library is
# BYTE-IDENTICAL between those two revs -- `git diff --name-only 0821366 49165ca`
# touches no file under internal/, bench/ or tools/ and no root .go file -- so the
# amd64 certificate transfers across a disclosed, library-neutral delta (gate scripts,
# README rows, and tracked archives only).
#
# The provision logs are NOT tracked: the arm64 one is 17 MB of OpenBLAS source-build
# output. Their digests are recorded here so the record is complete and checkable
# against a re-run, without putting 17 MB of compiler chatter in the repository.
06efe5b1767806d7024a2ac8b22674a75cc1ff8ee5d48f7a0273bfd68c0a927e  archive/cert-v0.2.0/gate-p5-amd64-0821366.log
61739227814adbf191a455e8d7be342da1923f88e04d5376c0783886fe21bbb0  archive/cert-v0.2.0/gate-p5-arm64-49165ca.log
# HOW TO VERIFY, and the two things that made the obvious command fail (#168, 2026-10-02):
#
#     cd <repo root> && shasum -a 256 -c archive/cert-v0.2.0/DIGESTS.sha256
#
# The paths below are repo-relative, so the repo root is the required cwd -- nothing in this
# file used to say so. And the two provision digests used to be written as checksum LINES with
# their filename in a `#` position; `shasum -c` does not treat `#` as a comment in the filename
# field, so it tried to open a file literally named `# cert-...` and the whole manifest exited 1
# while both tracked logs read OK. The digests were right and the artifact carrying them was not
# mechanically checkable -- which is exactly the class #168 names. They are plain commented text
# now, outside the checksum grammar, and the values are byte-for-byte the ones recorded at tag
# time: nothing about what the certificate attests has changed.
#
# provision logs -- NOT tracked (the arm64 one is 17 MB of OpenBLAS build output), digest only:
#   cert-amd64-provision-0821366.log
